<p>The Office for Budget Responsibility also says the cost by 2029-30 is around three times what was first assumed: {{ m.f("tl-cost-vs-earnings-2029-30") }} against {{ m.f("tl-cost-initial-assumption") }}. That compares two differences from earnings uprating. It does not mean State Pension spending is three times what was expected.</p>
{{ m.sourceNote("tl-cost-initial-assumption" | figure) }}

<h3>The saving from a change</h3>

{% call m.note("Past cost is not future saving", 4) %}
<p>The increases of past years are part of today's rates. Changing the rule does not reverse them. A change only affects increases from the date it starts, so the saving begins small and grows.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.scrollTable("Estimates of the saving from changing the yearly increase") %}
<table>
  <caption>Estimates of the saving from changing the yearly increase, compared with keeping the triple lock</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Change</th><th scope="col">Estimated saving</th><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Who made it</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for id, change, suffix in [
      ["saving-smoothed-rf-2030","Smoothed earnings link from 2027-28"," a year"],
      ["saving-earnings-gad-2031","Earnings link from April 2026",", built up over five years"],
      ["saving-earnings-ifs-2050","Pension kept at its present share of earnings from 2025"," a year"],
      ["saving-earnings-2075","Earnings link after 2030-31"," a year"],
      ["saving-cpi-2075","Prices link after 2030-31"," a year"]] %}
    {%- set fg = id | figure %}
    <tr><th scope="row">{{ change }}</th><td>{{ id | figShown }}{{ suffix }}</td><td>{{ fg.period_label }}</td><td>{{ fg.gross_net }}{% if fg.price_basis and fg.price_basis != "cash" %}. {{ fg.price_basis | upperFirst }}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ m.cite(fg.source) }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
